# ⎊::ZENS3N sites.map — read by the post-receive hook on minsky-vps
#
# format:  <satellites/ dir>   <domain> [alias ...]
#
# A line here means: publish this directory at these hostnames and let
# Caddy obtain a certificate for them. Only add a domain once its DNS
# actually points at the VPS, or the certificate request will fail.
#
# Delegated to ns1.zensen.systems, apex A -> 95.216.71.253:

sysgen.sh     sysgen.sh www.sysgen.sh
sysgen.dev    sysgen.dev www.sysgen.dev
3ox.dev       3ox.dev www.3ox.dev
# 3ox.me is served by /etc/caddy/sites.d/00-3oxme.caddy — apex,
# wildcard subdomains, and the /api/* gate all live there together.

# Still served by Squarespace — uncomment as each apex A record is
# repointed at 95.216.71.253 in the Knot zone:
#
# zensen.systems         zensen.systems www.zensen.systems
# zensen.live            zensen.live www.zensen.live
# zensen.solutions       zensen.solutions www.zensen.solutions
# zensen.store           zensen.store www.zensen.store
# zensenenterprise.com   zensenenterprises.com www.zensenenterprises.com
#
# note: the satellite dir is zensenenterprise.com (singular) but the
# domain you own is zensenenterprises.com (plural). Directory name is
# cosmetic; the domain column is what matters.
